<title>GERMANY: Dywidag sees &quot;appropriate&quot; dividend in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dywidag sees &quot;appropriate&quot; dividend in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Dyckerhoff &amp; Widmann AG (Dywidag) said on Tuesday its saw an &quot;appropriate&quot; full year dividend for 1996, compared to 10 marks in 1995.</p>
<p>Dywidag said its order book rose 11.6 percent to 3.487 billion marks in the first half of 1996 and said its first half total output was down 6.3 percent to 1.797 billion marks.  </p>
<p>The construction group said that the bad weather had led to the 6.3 percent drop in first half output and described the 11.6 rise in its order book as &quot;satisfactory&quot;, as it came against a backdrop of increased competition.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
